          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completeness"} Cauchy completeness
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bill+Lawvere"} Bill Lawvere
            in his influential paper
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Lawvere"} Metric spaces, generalized logic, and closed categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theorists
            as a concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
            in the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+completion"} idempotent completeness
          %p
            The basic idea is that the Cauchy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is the closure of a category under what are called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+limit"}> absolute limit
            s”, i.e., those
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            whatsoever. Equivalently, the Cauchy completion is the closure with respect to
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+colimit"} absolute colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{C}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            lies between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and its “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"}> free cocompletion
            ”, aka
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow \bar{C} \hookrightarrow Set^{C^{op}}
          %p
            and consists of the presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            dubbed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny
            by Lawvere, meaning those presheaves which are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object"} connected
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom_{Set^{C^{op}}}(F, -): Set^{C^{op}} \to Set
          %p
            preserves small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+closed+category"} monoidal closed category
          %p
            Lawvere defines a
            %strong point
            of the Cauchy completion of a small
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to be a
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: \mathbf{1} \to C
            (in other words, a
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1} \to V^{C^{op}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q: C \to \mathbf{1}
            right adjoint to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            (in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            of enriched bimodules, see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}
            is the unit
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: C^{op} \to V
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %strong Cauchy completion
            whose
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{C}
          %p
            As we will explain in more detail below,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable presheaves
            belong to the Cauchy completion, and so the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            factors through a full embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: C \to \bar{C}
          %p
            and we say the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %strong Cauchy complete
            if this embedding is an equivalence. We work through a few examples in the following section.
          %h2#InOrdinaryCategoryTheory In ordinary category theory
          %h3#in_terms_of_splitting_of_idempotents In terms of splitting of idempotents
          #CauchyCompletionByRetractsOfRepresentablePresheaves.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{C} \hookrightarrow [C^{op}, Set]
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              on the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representable functors
            %p
              This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              is called the
              %strong Cauchy completion
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#BorceuxDejean"}> BorceuxDejean, below theorem 1
            ).
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The Cauchy completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              satisfies the following properties
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi C
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                          %mo ↪
                          %mover
                            %mi C
                            %mo ¯
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow \overline{C}
              %li
                %p
                  every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi C
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+idempotent"} splits
              %li
                %p
                  the inclusion
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ↪
                        %mover
                          %mi C
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow \overline{C}
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                  precisely if already every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent"} idempotent
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  splits;
              %li
                %p
                  there is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mover
                            %mi C
                            %mo ¯
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [C^{op}, Set] \simeq [\overline{C}^{op}, Set]
                        \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#BorceuxDejean"}> BorceuxDejean, theorem 1
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              is small because
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              because the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              because it does so in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
              and because the composite of two retractions is a retraction.
            %p
              A retract of a representable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(c) \in [C^{op}, Set]
              induces an idempotent on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(c)
              and hence by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              an idempotent on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is already idempotent complete, this splits and produces a retraction of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and hence of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(C)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(c)
              is itself representable, therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≃
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \simeq \overline{C}
              in this case.
          %p
            Note that this construction of the Cauchy completion via the Yoneda embedding, we do not take
            %em all
            retracts of representables, since this would produce an equivalent replete subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
            which is only
            = succeed "." do
              %em essentially small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
            to provide a representative set of monomorphisms, amongst which we take the retracts to obtain a small full subcategory. For an alternative construction, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} Karoubi envelope
          %h3#InTermsOfTinyObjects In terms of tiny objects
          #CauchyComplIsFullSubcatOnTinyObjects.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The Cauchy completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op}, Set]
              on the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#BorceuxDejean"}> BorceuxDejean, prop. 2
            ).
          %h3#InTermsOfAbsoluteColimits In terms of absolute colimits
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The following conditions are equivalent for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is Cauchy complete;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  has all small
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+colimit"} absolute colimit
          %h3#InOrdinaryCatTheoryByProfunctors In terms of profunctors
          %p
            We discuss Cauchy completion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
            in terms of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            for the terminal category (single object, single morphism). Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              out of the point
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \simeq Func(*,C)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              is equivalent to the profunctor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Profunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [C^{op}, Set] \simeq Profunc(*, C)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In these terms the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow [C^{op}, Set]
              is the canonical inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Profunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func(*,C) \hookrightarrow Profunc(*,C)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Accordingly the Cauchy completion, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchyCompletionByRetractsOfRepresentablePresheaves"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the profunctor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Profunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{C} \hookrightarrow Profunc(*,C)
                    \\,.
          #CuachyCompByLeftAdjointProfunctor.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctor"} profunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : * &amp;#8696; C
              belongs to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              precisely if it has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#BorceuxDejean"}> BorceuxDejean, prop. 4
            ).
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  is Cauchy complete;
              %li
                %p
                  a profunctor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mi ⇸
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * &amp;#8696; C
                  has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  precisely if it is a functor;
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  a profunctor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mi ⇸
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A &amp;#8696; C
                  has a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  precisely if it is a functor;
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#BorceuxDejean"}> BorceuxDejean, theorem 2
            ).
          %h3#InOrdinaryCatTheoryByEssGeomMorphisms In terms of essential geometric morphisms
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            we say, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Set \stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\to}}}
                  [C,Set]
          %p
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential geometric morphism
            of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Set \to [C,Set]
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point+of+a+topos"} essential point
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set]
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            this is equivalently simply a single functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* : [C, Set] \to Set
            that preserves all small
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Topos
                    %mi ess
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi LRFunc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Topos_{ess}(Set,[C,Set])
                  \\simeq
                  LRFunc([C,Set], Set)
                  \\subset
                  Func([C,Set], Set)
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            on functors that have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
          #CauchyCompletionByEssentialPoints.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{C} \simeq Topos_{ess}(Set, [C,Set])^{op}
            %p
              of its Cauchy completion, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchyCompletionByRetractsOfRepresentablePresheaves"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set]
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              We first exhibit a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Topos
                        %mi ess
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                      %mo ↪
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos_{ess}(Set,[C,Set])^{op} \hookrightarrow \overline{C}
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\to}}} [C,Set]
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential geometric morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              and thus preserves all small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              and because every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              is the colimit over itself of the singleton set we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_! S \simeq \coprod_{s \in S} f_!(*)
            %p
              is fixed by a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copresheaf"} copresheaf
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F := f_!(*) \in [C, Set]
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_! \dashv f^*)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              then implies that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \in [C,Set]
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^* H \simeq Set(*, f^* H) \simeq [C,Set](f_! *, H)
                    \\simeq [C,Set](F,H)
            %p
              naturally in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^*(-) \simeq [C,Set](F,-) : Set \to [C,Set]
                    \\,.
            %p
              By assumption this has a further right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
              and hence preserves all
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
              it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in [C,Set]
              is a tiny object. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchyComplIsFullSubcatOnTinyObjects"}
              this means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              belongs to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C} \subset [C,Set]
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \Rightarrow g
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphisms"} geometric morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g : Set \to [C,Set]
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+transformation"} geometric transformation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ⇒
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* \Rightarrow g^*
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set](F,-) \Rightarrow [C,Set](G,-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              these are in bijection with morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to F
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set]
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Topos
                        %mi ess
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Set
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Topos_{ess}(Set,[C,Set])^{op} \subset \overline{C}
            %p
              The converse inclusion is now immediate by the same arguments: since the objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi C
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{C}
              are precisely the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in [C,Set]
              each of them corresponds to a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C,Set](F,-) : [C,Set] \to Set
              that has a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              of an essential geometric morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Set
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Set \to [C,Set]
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Cat
                    %mi Cauchy
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{Cauchy} \hookrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-2-category"} full sub-2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            on the Cauchy complete categories.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The 2-category of Cauchy complete categories is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-2-category"} full sub-2-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topos"} Topos
              with essential geometric morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi Cauchy
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cat_{Cauchy} \hookrightarrow Topos_{ess}
            %p
              exhibited by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-adjunction"} 2-adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Topos
                            %mi ess
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Set
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ↩
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Cat
                            %mi Cauchy
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Set
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi Cauchy
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([-,Set]
                    \\dashv
                    Topos_{ess}(Set,-)
                    )
                    
                    \:
                    Topos_{ess}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{Cat_{Cauchy}(-,Set)}{\hookleftarrow}}{\underset{Topos_{ess}(Set,-)}{\to}}
                    Cat_{Cauchy}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We first claim that when working with all categories instead of just the Cauchy complete categories there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-adjunction"} 2-adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Topos
                            %mi ess
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Set
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Set
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi Cat
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([-,Set]
                    \\dashv
                    Topos_{ess}(Set,-)
                    )
                    \:
                    Topos_{ess}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{[-,Set]}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{Topos_{ess}(Set,-)}{\to}}
                    Cat
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is exhibited by the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-categories"} hom-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Func
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi Topos
                              %mi ess
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Set
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi Func
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo ,
                            %mi LRFunc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi LRFunc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Func
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mo :
                            %mi LRFunc
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi C
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Topos
                              %mi ess
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi C
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo ,
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Func(C, Topos_{ess}(Set, E))
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Func(C, LRFunc(E, Set))
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    LRFunc(E, Func(C,Set)) =: LRFunc(E, [C,Set])
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Topos_{ess}([C,Set], E)
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in Cat
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Topos
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in Topos
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the first equivalence is by definition of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+geometric+morphism"} essential geometric morphism
              %li
                %p the second equivalence follows by observing that limits and colimits in presheaf categories are computed objectwise;
              %li
                %p the third equivalence is again the definition of essential geometric morphisms.
            %p
              Now by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchyCompletionByEssentialPoints"}
              we have that the components of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit
              of this adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Topos
                      %mi ess
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \to Topos_{ess}(Set,[C,Set])
            %p
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalences
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is Cauchy complete. This means that restricted along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi Cauchy
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{Cauchy} \hookrightarrow Cat
              the adjunction exhibits a coreflective embedding.
          %h2#InEnrichedCategoryTheory In enriched category theory
          %p
            We discuss Cauchy completion in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %a{:href => "InOrdinaryCategoryTheory"} above
            is the special case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒱
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V} :=
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            The key to the enriched version is the reformulation of ordinary Cauchy completion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            as discussed
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "InOrdinaryCatTheoryByProfunctors"} above
          %p As before, we have
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Every small
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is equivalent to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \simeq \mathcal{V}Func(I,C)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is the
              = succeed "-category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I(*,*) = I_{\mathcal{V}}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
            %p Also,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mi Profunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [C^{op}, \mathcal{V}] \simeq \mathcal{V}Profunc(I, C)
            %p
              and the canonical
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mi Profunc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{V}Func(I,C) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{V}Profunc(I,C)
            %p
              is the enriched
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a small
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
